{"defs":{"0":[{"path":["label"],"description":"Function name as serialised upstream. Values are resolved to concepts of ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-activation-scheme by context.jsonld. Note that the upstream label \"gaussian\" resolves to fcmact:logistic-of-square, which is what the implementation computes; see that block's description.\n","required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"]},{"path":["params"],"description":"Numeric parameters keyed by name. Which names are meaningful depends on `label` and is declared by fcmact:hasParameterName on the corresponding concept (`a`, `b`, `lambda` for the implemented functions).\n","required":true,"schema_type":"object","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"]}]},"properties":[{"path":["timespec_series"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/timeSpecSeries","description":"When each step applies. Must be pairwise non-overlapping, or the sequence cannot be ordered at all -- see description.md.\n","required":true,"schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-sequence"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/timeSpecSeries"},{"path":["timespec_series","_oneOf"],"sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-timespec"],"keyword":"oneOf"},{"path":["timespec_series","_oneOf","0"],"title":"a","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-timespec"],"keyword":"branch"},{"path":["timespec_series","_oneOf","0","type"],"id":"@type","required":true,"const":"pointtimespec","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-timespec"],"effectiveId":"@type"},{"path":["timespec_series","_oneOf","0","dt"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/instant","jsonld_type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime","description":"The instant the map and its solution apply to.","required":true,"sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-timespec"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/instant"},{"path":["timespec_series","_oneOf","1"],"title":"b","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-timespec"],"keyword":"branch"},{"path":["timespec_series","_oneOf","1","type"],"id":"@type","required":true,"const":"weekofyeartimespec","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-timespec"],"effectiveId":"@type"},{"path":["timespec_series","_oneOf","1","year"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/year","jsonld_type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer","required":true,"schema_type":"integer","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-timespec"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/year"},{"path":["timespec_series","_oneOf","1","week"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/week","jsonld_type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer","required":true,"schema_type":"integer","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-timespec"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/week"},{"path":["timespec_series","_oneOf","2"],"title":"c","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-timespec"],"keyword":"branch"},{"path":["timespec_series","_oneOf","2","type"],"id":"@type","required":true,"const":"monthofyeartimespec","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-timespec"],"effectiveId":"@type"},{"path":["timespec_series","_oneOf","2","year"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/year","jsonld_type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer","required":true,"schema_type":"integer","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-timespec"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/year"},{"path":["timespec_series","_oneOf","2","month"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/month","jsonld_type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer","description":"The 1..12 bound is ADDED here; upstream the field is a bare `Int` with no validation.\n","required":true,"schema_type":"integer","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-timespec"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/month"},{"path":["timespec_series","_oneOf","3"],"title":"d","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-timespec"],"keyword":"branch"},{"path":["timespec_series","_oneOf","3","type"],"id":"@type","required":true,"const":"rangetimespec","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-timespec"],"effectiveId":"@type"},{"path":["timespec_series","_oneOf","3","start"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/intervalStart","jsonld_type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime","required":true,"sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-timespec"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/intervalStart"},{"path":["timespec_series","_oneOf","3","stop"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/intervalStop","jsonld_type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime","required":true,"sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-timespec"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/intervalStop"},{"path":["fcm_series"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/mapSeries","description":"The map that held at each step. Repeating a structurally identical map at every step is normal; what usually changes between steps is a handful of edge weights.\n","required":true,"schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-sequence"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/mapSeries"},{"path":["fcm_series","graph"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/hasGraph","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/hasGraph"},{"path":["fcm_series","graph","vertices"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/hasNode","required":true,"schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/hasNode"},{"path":["fcm_series","graph","vertices","id"],"id":"@id","description":"Graph-local key of the concept, unique within the map, e.g. \"C1\" or \"Nd\". Referenced by the `src` and `dst` fields of edges. Not an IRI; the concept IRI, when known, belongs in the catalog record or in a future `concept` field (see description.md).\n","required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"effectiveId":"@id"},{"path":["fcm_series","graph","vertices","metadata"],"id":"@nest","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"effectiveId":"@nest"},{"path":["fcm_series","graph","vertices","metadata","description"],"id":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description","description":"Human-readable name of the concept, conventionally prefixed with the node key in square brackets, e.g. \"[C2] Stress Level\". Despite the field name this is a label rather than a description, and is mapped to skos:prefLabel.\n","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"effectiveId":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description"},{"path":["fcm_series","graph","edges"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/hasEdge","required":true,"schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/hasEdge"},{"path":["fcm_series","graph","edges","id"],"id":"@id","description":"Optional graph-local key of the edge, conventionally \"SRC->DST\".","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"effectiveId":"@id"},{"path":["fcm_series","graph","edges","src"],"description":"Key of the driving concept. Must equal the `id` of a vertex of the same map.","required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"]},{"path":["fcm_series","graph","edges","dst"],"description":"Key of the influenced concept. Must equal the `id` of a vertex of the same map.","required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"]},{"path":["fcm_series","graph","edges","weight"],"description":"Signed strength of the influence. Conventionally dimensionless in [-1, 1]; the convention is documented but NOT enforced upstream, and is not enforced here either. See description.md.\n","required":true,"schema_type":"number","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"]},{"path":["fcm_series","graph","edges","metadata"],"id":"@nest","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"effectiveId":"@nest"},{"path":["fcm_series","graph","edges","metadata","description"],"id":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description","description":"Free-text statement of the causal claim the edge encodes.","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"effectiveId":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description"},{"path":["fcm_series","graph","edges","metadata","provenance"],"description":"Free-text statement of where the weight came from. Marked as temporary upstream; expected to become a structured reference to the elicitation record (see description.md).\n","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"]},{"path":["fcm_series","graph","metadata"],"id":"@nest","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"effectiveId":"@nest"},{"path":["fcm_series","graph","metadata","description"],"id":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"effectiveId":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description"},{"path":["fcm_series","matrix"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/hasMatrix","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/hasMatrix"},{"path":["fcm_series","matrix","nodes"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/matrixNodes","jsonld_type":"@id","description":"Node keys, in the order used by both axes of `weights`.","required":true,"schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/matrixNodes"},{"path":["fcm_series","matrix","nodeLabels"],"description":"Optional map from node key to human-readable label.","schema_type":"object","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"]},{"path":["fcm_series","matrix","orientation"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/matrixOrientation","jsonld_type":"@vocab","description":"Declares that weights[i][j] is the influence of nodes[i] ON nodes[j]. Stated as a required constant rather than assumed, because the opposite convention is equally common and silently transposes the entire model. The solver applies the transpose at iteration time, computing f(W' x).\n","required":true,"const":"source-major","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/matrixOrientation"},{"path":["fcm_series","matrix","weights"],"description":"Square matrix of signed weights; absent influences are 0.","required":true,"schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"]},{"path":["fcm_series","activation_spec"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/hasActivationSpec","required":true,"sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/hasActivationSpec"},{"path":["fcm_series","activation_spec","_then"],"sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"keyword":"then"},{"path":["fcm_series","activation_spec","mode"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/activationMode","jsonld_type":"@vocab","required":true,"enum":["homogeneous","heterogeneous"],"sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/activationMode"},{"path":["fcm_series","activation_spec","homogeneous"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/homogeneousActivation","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"ref":"0","effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/homogeneousActivation"},{"path":["fcm_series","activation_spec","heterogeneous"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/heterogeneousActivation","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"ref":"0","effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/heterogeneousActivation"},{"path":["fcm_series","metadata"],"id":"@nest","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"effectiveId":"@nest"},{"path":["fcm_series","metadata","description"],"id":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm"],"effectiveId":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description"},{"path":["solution_series"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/solutionSeries","description":"The solution computed from the map at the same index. A step's solution is index-aligned with its own map's vertex order, not with any other step's.\n","required":true,"schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-sequence"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/solutionSeries"},{"path":["solution_series","_then"],"sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-solution"],"keyword":"then"},{"path":["solution_series","_then","centroids"],"sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-solution"]},{"path":["solution_series","_then","maxdists"],"sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-solution"]},{"path":["solution_series","centroids"],"description":"One entry per distinct equilibrium found. Each entry is a state vector: one value per concept node, in the vertex order of the map that was solved. Typically there is exactly one entry, but a map with several basins of attraction yields several.\n","required":true,"schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-solution"]},{"path":["solution_series","maxdists"],"description":"Componentwise error bound for the correspondingly-indexed centroid: for each component, the spread (max - min) across the cluster of trial endpoints that centroid represents. Index-aligned with `centroids` element by element AND component by component.\n","required":true,"schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-solution"]},{"path":["solution_series","b_success"],"id":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/hasFiniteEquilibria","jsonld_type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean","description":"True when the map settles on finitely many discrete stable points. When false the solution carries no usable information and must be ignored.\nNote that no code path in upstream v0.1.0 ever sets this to false -- both constructors hardcode `true`. Treat a `true` here as \"not yet contradicted\" rather than as a positive assertion of convergence. See description.md.\n","required":true,"schema_type":"boolean","sources":["bblocks://ogc.hosted.seadots.fcm-solution"],"effectiveId":"https://w3id.org/ogc/hosted/seadots/fcm/hasFiniteEquilibria"}]}